From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Garcia-Madico Portabella <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 21:48:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/37] ASoC: qdsp6: q6voice: do not rebuild the whole session
 on a device switch by default

switch_full_session was turned on to bring a call back to a Bluetooth
headset with audio. The silent return turned out to be the SLIMBus manager
keeping the stream's channels, fixed by removing them when the stream is
disabled (qcom-ngd-ctrl remove_channels), and rebuilding MVM, CVS and the
vocproc coincided with an ADSP crash when moving a call to the speaker.

On the Nothing Phone (1), with channel removal on, a vocproc-only move takes
a call from the headset to the earpiece and back with audio both ways
(measured 2026-09-13). A boot service was writing N; make it the default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c
index e2a3d8f45..e9377f34e 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c
@@ -77,8 +77,15 @@ static void q6voice_apply_rx_volume(struct device *dev, struct q6voice_session *
  * from scratch. With this set, a move tears the three sessions down and builds
  * them again against the new ports. Writable, so that both ways can be
  * compared between calls: /sys/module/q6voice/parameters/switch_full_session
+ *
+ * Off by default. The silent return turned out to be the bus manager keeping
+ * the stream's channels (see remove_channels in qcom-ngd-ctrl), not the
+ * session, and rebuilding the whole session coincided with an ADSP crash when
+ * moving a call to the speaker. On the Nothing Phone (1), with channel removal
+ * on, a vocproc-only move brings a call back to the headset with audio both
+ * ways (measured 2026-09-13).
  */
-static bool switch_full_session = true;
+static bool switch_full_session;
 module_param(switch_full_session, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(switch_full_session,
 		 "rebuild MVM, CVS and vocproc (not only the vocproc) when a call changes device");
